<div class="start-card"><p><strong>Requires:</strong> stages 01–02 submitted and images pushed.</p></div>
<h2 id="ready">Wait, then configure</h2>
{{snippet:commands.sh:configure}}
<p><code>03-ready.sh</code> waits for ARM, a Ready node and the PostgreSQL <code>VECTOR</code> allowlist. <code>04-configure.sh</code> assigns roles, federation, kubelet AcrPull, KEDA's separate identity and ordinary settings.</p>
<details class="optional" id="identity"><summary>How identity, settings and secrets connect</summary>
<figure class="flow" aria-label="Identity and configuration architecture"><div class="flow-node"><strong>AKS service account</strong>Client-ID annotation + Pod label</div><span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><div class="flow-node"><strong>Federation</strong>OIDC → Entra token</div><span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><div class="flow-node"><strong>App Configuration</strong>Endpoints and settings</div><span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><div class="flow-node"><strong>Key Vault</strong>Read passwords</div><figcaption>Functions uses managed identity directly. All apps read settings/secrets at startup; changes require restart.</figcaption></figure>
<table><thead><tr><th>Mechanism</th><th>Workshop use</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Key Vault</td><td>PostgreSQL and Products sign-in passwords</td></tr><tr><td>App Configuration</td><td>Endpoints, model names, retrieval count, chunk size</td></tr><tr><td>ConfigMap</td><td>Non-secret App Configuration endpoint/label</td></tr><tr><td>Kubernetes Secret</td><td>Endpoint TLS certificate/private key</td></tr><tr><td>Environment variables</td><td>Bootstrap settings and SDK identity metadata</td></tr><tr><td>Managed/workload identity</td><td>Short-lived tokens; Azure roles grant access separately</td></tr></tbody></table>
<h3>Bootstrap and federation</h3><p>Applications start with <code>APP_CONFIG_ENDPOINT</code> and label <code>workshop</code>. App Configuration provides service settings and the vault URI; Key Vault supplies passwords. AKS requires the service-account annotation <code>azure.workload.identity/client-id</code>, Pod label <code>azure.workload.identity/use: "true"</code> and a federated credential matching issuer/subject/audience. See {{file:k8s/products.yaml}} and {{file:scripts/04-configure.sh}}.</p>
</details>
<h2 id="schema">Inspect the Flyway migration</h2>
<p>{{file:apps/products/src/main/resources/db/migration/V1__products_and_messages.sql}} creates the schema when Products starts. Flyway records versions/checksums; reruns validate existing migrations.</p>
<details class="optional" id="consistency"><summary>Schema and upload consistency</summary>
<ul><li>Both document/question embeddings use the same deployment and <code>vector(1536)</code>. Retrieval uses exact cosine distance <code>&lt;=&gt;</code>; no ANN index.</li><li>Chunk key: <code>(manual_id, chunk_index)</code>. Chunks + ready state commit atomically.</li><li>Question + outbox commit together; replies/results persist by request ID.</li></ul>
<p id="ordering">The product row commits <em>before</em> blob upload. Failed uploads persist failure; abandoned waiting work times out. Manuals are immutable.</p>
</details>
<details class="optional"><summary>Database simplification</summary><p>The workshop shares the <code>workshopadmin</code> database owner across migrations/apps, with its password in Key Vault. Production should separate runtime/migration roles. Private DNS/VNet access keeps PostgreSQL private; your laptop normally cannot connect directly.</p></details>
<div class="verification" id="verify"><strong>Verification:</strong> node Ready, VECTOR allowlisted, settings/roles configured. Flyway runs in the next chapter.</div>
<details class="optional"><summary>Troubleshooting</summary><ul><li><strong>Database DNS/connectivity:</strong> check the private zone's VNet link and delegated subnet; do not open an internet-wide firewall rule.</li><li><strong>Vault/settings 403:</strong> check workload principal, role scope and propagation; CLI sign-in does not configure the Pod.</li><li><strong>Extension failure:</strong> allowlist VECTOR; create SQL extension <code>vector</code> as the database owner.</li><li><strong>KEDA authentication:</strong> inspect its own identity/federation, independently of the worker.</li></ul></details>
